# secretscan path allowances — root-relative globs.
# site/vendor/ holds pinned, unmodified third-party bytes (ADR
# 2026-08-08-0450, ADR 2026-08-08-0546) — minified/bundled JS and CSS,
# not content this repo authored. Minified identifiers and packed
# numeric literal tables read exactly like the entropy/assigned-secret
# shapes this scanner looks for; tools/vendor_check.py is what actually
# guards this directory (a sha256 pin per file, checked every run), so
# leaving it in scope here would only ever produce noise, never signal.
site/vendor/**

# tools/vendor-manifest.json's entire content is npm integrity hashes
# (sha512, base64) and per-file sha256 pins — high-entropy strings by
# definition, and every future re-vendor adds more of them. The real
# guard on this file is vendor_check.py's exact-value comparison, not a
# shape scan; a per-line allow-marker here would just have to be
# re-added on every pin update, for a file where the "finding" is the
# file's whole and permanent purpose.
tools/vendor-manifest.json

# NOTICE duplicates those same integrity hashes in prose form (the
# compliance record a human reads, next to the manifest a script
# reads) — same high-entropy false positive, same reason, and it grows
# by one hash per future vendored library.
NOTICE
